  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "The kanji are just given for reference. Kana spelling is normal today. \nThese words are part of what is called kosoado. The ko, so and a indicate the relation to the speaker, the re turns them into the pronouns for a certain object.\nThe most important thing to remember is that you cannot these words to say, for example, \"I want this apple\" = \"kore ringo ga hoshii.\" That is wrong. You can only use them for \"I want this.\"\n(\"this apple\" would be \"kono ringo\")",
      "html": "The kanji are just given for reference. Kana spelling is normal today. <br/>These words are part of what is called kosoado. The ko, so and a indicate the relation to the speaker, the re turns them into the pronouns for a certain object.<br/>The most important thing to remember is that you cannot these words to say, for example, \"I want this apple\" = \"kore ringo ga hoshii.\" That is wrong. You can only use them for \"I want this.\"<br/>(\"this apple\" would be \"kono ringo\")",
      "credits_raw": "blutorange",
      "content_sha256": "8e2c706155e6701be6f4e5d31c01edc65ff406ce8cb8a0ce53a40ee5b70f12a9",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
